---
# Starlight's <Icon> (@astrojs/starlight/user-components/Icon.astro): {% icon "open-book" %},
# {% icon "seti:c-sharp", label: "C#", size: "1.5rem", color: "var(--sl-color-text-accent)", class: "icon" %}.
# The path data comes from the sprite assets/icons.svg (scripts/icons-sprite.mjs): every Starlight icon plus the
# devicon/mdi/material-icon-theme icons the site uses, ids as named here. No viewBox on the outer svg: the symbol's
# own viewBox scales into it. Starlight's define:vars sets --sl-icon-size (default 1em) and --sl-icon-color.
# Root class: cid-sl-icon.
# `params` (every shortcode declares it): the named arguments the shortcode reads. A declared parameter that the
# call does not pass must resolve to nil, not to the page's value of the same name (`title`, `description`,
# `lang`, `icon`...): see the M3 report (Douze shortcode model, plan 2.5).
args: [name]
params: [label, size, color, class]
---
<svg {% if label %}aria-label="{{ label | escape }}"{% else %}aria-hidden="true"{% endif %} class="cid-sl-icon{% if class %} {{ class }}{% endif %}" width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" style="--sl-icon-size: {{ size | default: '1em' }};{% if color %} --sl-icon-color: {{ color }};{% endif %}"><use href="/assets/icons.svg#{{ name }}"></use></svg>